From 6ac4579e4b62420e35b99fabbf3bbf3166ca7edf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Francesco Pham <francesco.pham1@h-partners.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:31:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] render_service: zero-initialise the logical display content
 rect

RSLogicalDisplayRenderNode::contentRect_ is a plain Rect with no
initialiser, and DMS only sets it through SetPhysicalVisibleMaskToDisplayNode
(devices with a physical display mask). Everywhere else it keeps whatever
the heap held when the node was allocated.

RSSurfaceCaptureTaskParallel::CreatePixelMapByDisplayNode sizes a display
capture from that rect whenever w and h are both positive. With leftover
pointer bytes in it (seen on the x86 emulator: "contentRect valid, width:
958612024, height: 32641") PixelMap::Create fails, "pixelMap_ is nullptr",
and every snapshot_display / screenshot of that display fails at once for
the lifetime of the display node. Whether it happens depends on the heap
state at boot, so it hit about one boot in four on the CI emulator and
none on others.

Initialise it to {0, 0, 0, 0} like RSLogicalDisplayRenderParams already
does, so an unset rect means "use the node size".

Change-Id: Ia35faa5d1460dbaec1eb6c2bab60137259c97b67
Signed-off-by: Francesco Pham <francesco.pham1@h-partners.com>
---
 .../include/pipeline/rs_logical_display_render_node.h           | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/rosen/modules/render_service_base/include/pipeline/rs_logical_display_render_node.h b/rosen/modules/render_service_base/include/pipeline/rs_logical_display_render_node.h
index 17419e1083..4c267febff 100644
--- a/rosen/modules/render_service_base/include/pipeline/rs_logical_display_render_node.h
+++ b/rosen/modules/render_service_base/include/pipeline/rs_logical_display_render_node.h
@@ -234,7 +234,7 @@ private:
     void InitRenderParams() override;
 
     ScreenId screenId_ = INVALID_SCREEN_ID;
-    Rect contentRect_;
+    Rect contentRect_ = {0, 0, 0, 0};
     std::vector<Occlusion::Rect> topSurfaceOpaqueRects_;
 
     // bounds rotation
-- 
